    <div class="puzzle" id="puzzle2-2">
    <h3>Challenge 2: Obtain a Kerboeros ticket</h3>

    To help with managing users and credential security, we use <a href="https://web.mit.edu/Kerberos/">a network authentication protocol called Kerberos</a>
    <p>
    Now that you are logged in to your shell, you are ready to
    <a href="https://web.mit.edu/Kerberos/krb5-latest/doc/user/tkt_mgmt.html#obtaining-tickets-with-kinit">obtain your first set of Kerberos credentials</a>.
    This will help you navigate around the network without having to type your password over and over. A Kerberos ticket is also useful
    when you need to elevate your priviliges on a host.
    <p>
    Use the &quot;kinit&quot; command to obtain a ticket. You can check if you did it right by running the tool in your home folder called &quot;check_ticket&quot;
    <p>
    <em>HINT: your passwd for user &quot;sly&quot; was set to 123 the other day</em>

