<div class="center">
    <div class="puzzle" id="puzzle2-3">
    <h3>Challenge 3: The Gopher server</h3>

    Now it's time to check out some of the things on the lab network that you can interact with.
    <p>
    Have you ever heard of <a href="https://www.howtogeek.com/661871/the-web-before-the-web-a-look-back-at-gopher/">a protocol named Gopher</a>?
    It was created by some very famous people, <a href="https://www.w3.org/People/Berners-Lee/">including Sir Tim Berners-Lee</a> at
    <a href="https://home.cern/">CERN in Switzerland</a>.
    <p>
    Try to log in to another host now to run Gopher. 
    
    <ol>
    <li>Use the command <em>&quot;ssh -XK -l sly node0&quot;</em> to access node0. </li>
    <li>Become the root user by typing the command &quot;ksu&quot;. Your prompt should change to  a hash mark.</li>
    <li>Search for the gopher client package &quot;apt-cache search gopher&quot; and install it.</li>
    <li>Type exit to change back to your regular user. Use the Gopher client to access &quot;gopher://www.bitsmasher.net&quot;</li>
    </ol>
