<div class="center">
    <div class="puzzle" id="puzzle2-4">
    <h3>Challenge 4: The Time Server (NTP)</h3>
    Having a precise source of time is crucial in a network like ours where computers must work together in a &quot;tightly-coupled&quot; fashion.
    Software builds, log correlation, cluster message passing and more all rely on a stable and accurate source of time.
    <p>
    <ol>
    <li>Use the &quot;ntpq&quot; command to view the source of time for the host you are on, node0. HINT: You might need to look at the flags for the command.</li>
    <li>You sould be able to see the name of the time server in the output of the ntpq command.</li>
    <li>Use &quot;nslookup&quot; or &quot;whois&quot; to determine the IPv4 address of the NTP server.</li>
    <li>Run the file &quot;check_ip&quot; in your home directory to check your answer.</li>
    </ol>
